# Y-junction mixer — curved arms, so two streams lie down side by side.
#
# Both inlet arms curve so they arrive at the junction running parallel. The
# streams merge as co-flowing laminae rather than colliding head-on, which is
# what you want for cells, emulsions, or anything a collision would damage.
# It is also the slowest-mixing merge, because nothing stretches the interface.
#
# Demonstrates `via`: two cubic control points turn a segment into a bezier.

chip "Y-junction mixer"
printer standard-4k
size 36 x 44
base 4
wall 2
edge-spacing 3
split two-piece at 2
channel 0.8 x 0.5 rect

port inletA at 9,37  luer-slip inlet water 10
port inletB at 27,37 luer-slip inlet water 10
port outlet at 18,6  luer-slip outlet

node junction at 18,28

path inletA -> junction via (9,33) (18,32)
path inletB -> junction via (27,33) (18,32)
path junction -> (18,21) -> (18,14) -> outlet
